<title>JAPAN: NAMCO buys Irish game machine factory - paper.</title>
<headline>NAMCO buys Irish game machine factory - paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>NAMCO Ltd has purchased a game machine factory in Ireland from Atari Games of the United States, a Japanese business paper reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The factory has the capacity to make 150 to 200 game machines per day, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun said.</p>
<p>With the newly acquired factory, NAMCO hopes to take advantage of the growing European market for game machines, it said.</p>
<p>It did not mention the purchase price.</p>
</text>
